# Line endings, declared rather than guessed.
#
# Without this file git falls back to its binary-detection heuristic plus core.autocrlf, which
# is what printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" during the first add. The stored blobs happened
# to already be LF, so nothing was wrong yet - but the policy was implicit, and an implicit one
# is what makes a whole file show as changed because someone's editor saved it differently.
#
# Pinned to LF rather than text=auto on purpose: text=auto keeps converting per platform, so a
# Windows checkout would carry CRLF while a macOS one carries LF, and the two disagree in every
# diff after that. This project is TypeScript bundled by esbuild and runs the same tests on
# desktop and iOS Obsidian, so there is no build step anywhere that needs CRLF.
* text eol=lf

# Generated and vendored paths: never line-ending candidates, never diff noise. Written with
# an explicit /** because a trailing slash is gitignore syntax, not gitattributes - a bare
# `node_modules/` line here silently matches nothing and the `*` rule above wins instead.
node_modules/** text=no
.obsidian/** text=no

# Anything that is bytes to us, listed rather than left to a guess: the `* text` rule above
# would otherwise try to normalise these, and rewriting line endings inside a PNG breaks it.
# SVG is deliberately absent - artwork in this repo is text and should stay normalised.
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
*.pdf -text
*.zip -text
*.ttf -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text

# .gitignore stays text so its own comments stay readable in a diff.
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
